label: Solar flares
events: solar flare events
archive: solar flare archive
source caveat: Lists every flare on the Sun. Only one on the receiver's sunlit side raises the ionization above it.
below the scale: Below R1
no end time: end not published
receiver sunlit: Receiver: sunlit side
receiver on the night side: Receiver: night side
plot hover: Solar flares from the NASA DONKI catalog, marked at their peak.
One vertical line at each peak, coloured by class, X ten times M.
More: 'How do solar flares affect GNSS?' in Settings.
missing key: The NASA DONKI endpoint needs an API key of your own. Without one GeoTrace requests no flares. Registering at https://api.nasa.gov is free and the key arrives by email.
attribution: Solar flare events from the NASA DONKI catalog.
publisher: https://ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/tools/DONKI/
key signup: https://api.nasa.gov
